{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>And the Amalekite.</b> By the same measure that the spies frightened them with Amalek, by it the Holy One frightened them." "<b>And the Canaanite.</b> He is an Amorite; he is a Canaanite." "<b> Dwelling in the valley.</b> And further on it is written: 'וירד העמלקי והכנעני היושב בהר ההוא' — rather, one may answer: the majority of them were dwelling in the valley and the minority of them on the mountain, and that minority fought against them. And a proof for this: as it is written 'היושב בהר ההוא' — by implication there are some of them dwelling in another place. Or perhaps they were dwelling in the valley, and when they heard that the children of Israel were coming against them, they went up on the mountain and ambushed them there — and we find the language of 'dwelling' used in connection with ambush, as it is written: 'יושב במארב חצרים.'" "<b>Tomorrow, turn and journey for yourselves.</b> 'Tomorrow' here means after some time, for they stayed in Kadesh many days before they began to go around Mount Seir. And it is an illustration, as in 'כי ישאלך בנך מחר.'" "<b>The wilderness by way of the Sea of Reeds.</b> To go around Mount Seir, as we find in the section of Devarim, in order to fulfill the decree of 'ובניכם יהיו רועים במדבר ארבעים שנה.'"], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:17:58.989234683Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}